#: ../../library/turtle.rst:223 ../../library/turtle.rst:245
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:269 ../../library/turtle.rst:295
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:395 ../../library/turtle.rst:417
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:440 ../../library/turtle.rst:491
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:763 ../../library/turtle.rst:1304
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1712 ../../library/turtle.rst:1713
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1714 ../../library/turtle.rst:1715
msgid "a number"
msgstr "um número"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:225
msgid ""
"Move the turtle forward by the specified *distance*, in the direction the "
"turtle is headed."
msgstr ""
"Move a tartaruga para frente pela *distance* especificada, na direção em que "
"a tartaruga está indo."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:228
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(25)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(25.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(-75)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-50.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(25)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(25.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(-75)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-50.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:247
msgid ""
"Move the turtle backward by *distance*, opposite to the direction the turtle "
"is headed. The turtle's heading does not change."
msgstr ""
"Move a tartaruga para trás por *distance*, na direção oposta à direção em "
"que a tartaruga está indo. A direção da tartaruga não muda."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:256
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.backward(30)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-30.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.backward(30)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-30.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:271
msgid ""
"Turn the turtle right by the specified *angle*. The angle is measured in "
"degrees by default; the unit can be changed with :func:`degrees` or :func:"
"`radians`. How the heading is measured depends on the turtle mode, see :func:"
"`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Gira a tartaruga para direita pelo ângulo *angle* especificado. Por padrão, "
"o ângulo é medido em graus; a unidade pode ser alterada com :func:`degrees` "
"ou :func:`radians`. A forma como a direção é medida depende do modo da "
"tartaruga; consulte :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:282
msgid ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.right(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"337.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.right(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"337.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:297
msgid ""
"Turn the turtle left by the specified *angle*. The angle is measured in "
"degrees by default; the unit can be changed with :func:`degrees` or :func:"
"`radians`. How the heading is measured depends on the turtle mode, see :func:"
"`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Gira a tartaruga para esquerda pelo ângulo *angle* especificado. Por padrão, "
"o ângulo é medido em graus; a unidade pode ser alterada com :func:`degrees` "
"ou :func:`radians`. A forma como a direção é medida depende do modo da "
"tartaruga; consulte :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:308
msgid ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.left(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.left(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:322
msgid "a number or a pair/vector of numbers"
msgstr "um número ou um par/vetor de números"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:323 ../../library/turtle.rst:355
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:356 ../../library/turtle.rst:492
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1940 ../../library/turtle.rst:1941
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1942 ../../library/turtle.rst:1988
msgid "a number or ``None``"
msgstr "um número ou ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:325
msgid ""
"Move the turtle to an absolute position. If *y* is ``None``, *x* must be a "
"pair of coordinates or a :class:`Vec2D`, for example as returned by :func:"
"`pos`. If the pen is down, a line is drawn. The turtle's heading does not "
"change."
msgstr ""
"Move a tartaruga para uma posição absoluta. Se *y* for ``None``, *x* deve "
"ser um par de coordenadas ou um :class:`Vec2D`, como, por exemplo, o valor "
"retornado por :func:`pos`. Se a caneta estiver abaixada, uma linha é "
"desenhada. A orientação da tartaruga não muda."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:336
msgid ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(60,30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,30.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto((20,80))\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,80.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(tp)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(60,30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,30.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto((20,80))\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,80.00)\n"
">>> turtle.goto(tp)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:357
msgid "a boolean"
msgstr "um valor booleano"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:359
msgid ""
"Teleport, or instantly move, the turtle to an absolute position. Unlike :"
"func:`goto`, no line is drawn. If *x* or *y* is not given, that coordinate "
"is kept as it is. The turtle's heading does not change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:363
msgid ""
"If the turtle is filling a shape, the shape drawn so far is finished and "
"filled before teleporting, and filling starts again at the new position. "
"Pass ``fill_gap=True`` to keep filling one shape instead. The teleport then "
"counts as an edge of the shape, as it would with :func:`goto`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:374
msgid ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(60)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(y=10)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(20, 30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,30.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(60)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(y=10)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(20, 30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,30.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:397
msgid "Set the turtle's x coordinate to *x*. The y coordinate is unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Define a coordenada x da tartaruga para *x*. A coordenada y permanece "
"inalterada."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:405
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,240.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setx(10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(10.00,240.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,240.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setx(10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(10.00,240.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:419
msgid "Set the turtle's y coordinate to *y*. The x coordinate is unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Define a coordenada y da tartaruga para *y*. A coordenada x permanece "
"inalterada."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:427
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,40.00)\n"
">>> turtle.sety(-10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-10.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,40.00)\n"
">>> turtle.sety(-10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-10.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:442
msgid ""
"Set the turtle's heading to *to_angle*. Here are some common directions in "
