msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1397
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-click events on this turtle. *fun* is called with the "
"coordinates of the clicked point on the canvas. If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed. *btn* is the number of the mouse button and "
"defaults to 1, the left mouse button. If *add* is ``True``, a new binding is "
"added, otherwise it replaces a former binding. Example for the anonymous "
"turtle, that is, the procedural way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1404
msgid ""
">>> def turn(x, y):\n"
"...     left(180)\n"
"...\n"
">>> onclick(turn)  # Now clicking into the turtle will turn it.\n"
">>> onclick(None)  # event-binding will be removed"
msgstr ""
">>> def turn(x, y):\n"
"...     left(180)\n"
"...\n"
">>> onclick(turn)  # Agora, clicar na tartaruga irá girá-la.\n"
">>> onclick(None)  # a associação de eventos será removida"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1416 ../../library/turtle.rst:1441
msgid ""
"a function with two arguments which will be called with the coordinates of "
"the clicked point on the canvas"
msgstr ""
"um função com dois argumento que serão chamados com as coordenadas do ponto "
"clicado na tela"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1418 ../../library/turtle.rst:1443
msgid "number of the mouse-button, defaults to 1 (left mouse button)"
msgstr "número do botão do mouse, o padrão é 1 (botão esquerdo do mouse)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1419 ../../library/turtle.rst:1444
msgid ""
"``True`` or ``False`` -- if ``True``, a new binding will be added, otherwise "
"it will replace a former binding"
msgstr ""
"``True`` ou ``False`` -- se ``True``, uma nova ligação será adicionada; caso "
"contrário, ela substituirá uma ligação antiga"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1422
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-button-release events on this turtle.  If *fun* is "
"``None``, existing bindings are removed."
msgstr ""
"Vincule *fun* aos eventos de liberação do botão do mouse nesta tartaruga.  "
"Se *fun* for ``None``, as associações existentes serão removidas."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1425
msgid ""
">>> class MyTurtle(Turtle):\n"
"...     def glow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"red\")\n"
"...     def unglow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"\")\n"
"...\n"
">>> turtle = MyTurtle()\n"
">>> turtle.onclick(turtle.glow)     # clicking on turtle turns fillcolor "
"red,\n"
">>> turtle.onrelease(turtle.unglow) # releasing turns it to transparent."
msgstr ""
">>> class MyTurtle(Turtle):\n"
"...     def glow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"red\")\n"
"...     def unglow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"\")\n"
"...\n"
">>> turtle = MyTurtle()\n"
">>> turtle.onclick(turtle.glow)     # clicar na tartaruga torna o "
"preenchimento vermelho,\n"
">>> turtle.onrelease(turtle.unglow) # .liberar a transforma em transparente"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1447
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-move events on this turtle.  If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed."
msgstr ""
"Vincule *fun* a eventos de movimentação do mouse nessa tartaruga.  Se *fun* "
"for ``None``, as associações existentes serão removidas."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1450
msgid ""
"Remark: Every sequence of mouse-move-events on a turtle is preceded by a "
"mouse-click event on that turtle."
msgstr ""
"Observação: Cada sequência de eventos de movimento do mouse em uma tartaruga "
"é precedida por um evento de clique do mouse naquela tartaruga."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1453
msgid ">>> turtle.ondrag(turtle.goto)"
msgstr ">>> turtle.ondrag(turtle.goto)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1458
msgid ""
"Subsequently, clicking and dragging the Turtle will move it across the "
"screen thereby producing handdrawings (if pen is down)."
msgstr ""
"Posteriormente, clicar e arrastar a Tartaruga a moverá pela tela, produzindo "
"desenhos à mão (se a caneta estiver deitada)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1463
msgid "Special Turtle methods"
msgstr "Métodos Especiais da Tartaruga"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1467
msgid ""
"Record the vertices of a polygon drawn in the ``with turtle.poly():`` block. "
"The first and last vertices will be connected."
msgstr ""
"Registra os vértices de um polígono desenhado no bloco ``with turtle.poly():"
"``. O primeiro e o último vértices serão conectados."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1470
msgid ""
">>> with turtle.poly():\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)\n"
"...     turtle.right(60)\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)"
msgstr ""
">>> with turtle.poly():\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)\n"
"...     turtle.right(60)\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1483
msgid ""
"Start recording the vertices of a polygon. The current turtle position is "
"the first vertex of the polygon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1489
msgid ""
"Stop recording the vertices of a polygon. The current turtle position is the "
"last vertex of the polygon. This will be connected with the first vertex."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1495
msgid "Return the last recorded polygon."
msgstr "Retorna o último polígono registrado."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1497
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.begin_poly()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(100)\n"
">>> turtle.left(20)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.end_poly()\n"
">>> p = turtle.get_poly()\n"
">>> register_shape(\"myFavouriteShape\", p)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.begin_poly()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(100)\n"
">>> turtle.left(20)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.end_poly()\n"
">>> p = turtle.get_poly()\n"
">>> register_shape(\"myFavouriteShape\", p)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1514
msgid ""
"Create and return a clone of the turtle. The clone has the same position, "
"heading and turtle properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1517
msgid ""
">>> leonel = Turtle()\n"
">>> marco = leonel.clone()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1527
msgid "Return the Turtle object itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1529
msgid ""
"Call ``getturtle()`` to get the turtle used by functions such as :func:"
"`forward` and :func:`left`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1532
msgid ""
">>> pet = getturtle()\n"
">>> pet.fd(50)\n"
">>> pet\n"
"<turtle.Turtle object at 0x...>"
msgstr ""
">>> pet = getturtle()\n"
">>> pet.fd(50)\n"
">>> pet\n"
"<turtle.Turtle object at 0x...>"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1543
msgid ""
"Return the :class:`TurtleScreen` object the turtle is drawing on. "
"TurtleScreen methods can then be called for that object."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o objeto :class:`TurtleScreen` no qual a tartaruga está sendo "
"desenhada. Os métodos de TurtleScreen podem então ser chamados para este "
"objeto."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1546
msgid ""
">>> ts = turtle.getscreen()\n"
">>> ts\n"
"<turtle._Screen object at 0x...>\n"
">>> ts.bgcolor(\"pink\")"
msgstr ""
">>> ts = turtle.getscreen()\n"
">>> ts\n"
"<turtle._Screen object at 0x...>\n"
">>> ts.bgcolor(\"pink\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1559
msgid ""
"Set or disable the undo buffer. If *size* is an integer, an empty undo "
"buffer of the given size is installed. *size* is the maximum number of "
"turtle actions that can be undone by :func:`undo`. If *size* is ``None``, "
"the undo buffer is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1564
msgid ">>> turtle.setundobuffer(42)"
msgstr ">>> turtle.setundobuffer(42)"

