msgid "Screen methods and functions"
msgstr "Métodos e funções de janela"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1587
msgid ""
"Most of the examples in this section refer to a TurtleScreen instance called "
"``screen``."
msgstr ""
"A maioria dos exemplos desta seção se refere a uma instância de TurtleScreen "
"chamada ``screen``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1598
msgid "Window control"
msgstr "Controle da Janela"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1604
msgid "Return or set the background color of the TurtleScreen."
msgstr "Retorna ou define a cor de fundo do TurtleScreen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1608
msgid "``bgcolor()``"
msgstr "``bgcolor()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1609
msgid ""
"Return the current background color as a color specification string or as a "
"tuple (see example).  May be used as input to another :func:`color`, :func:"
"`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` or :func:`bgcolor` call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1614
msgid "``bgcolor(colorstring)``"
msgstr "``bgcolor(colorstring)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1615
msgid ""
"Set the background color to *colorstring*, which is a Tk color specification "
"string, such as ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"``, or ``\"#33cc8c\"``."
msgstr ""
"Define a cor de fundo como *colorstring*, que é uma string de especificação "
"de cor Tk, como ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"`` ou ``\"#33cc8c\"``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1618
msgid "``bgcolor((r, g, b))``"
msgstr "``bgcolor((r, g, b))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1619
msgid ""
"Set the background color to the RGB color represented by the tuple of *r*, "
"*g*, and *b*. Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode, "
"where colormode is either 1.0 or 255 (see :func:`colormode`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1624
msgid "``bgcolor(r, g, b)``"
msgstr "``bgcolor(r, g, b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1625
msgid ""
"Set the background color to the RGB color represented by *r*, *g*, and *b*. "
"Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1628
msgid ""
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"'orange'\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"#800080\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"(128.0, 0.0, 128.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"'orange'\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"#800080\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"(128.0, 0.0, 128.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1641
msgid ""
"a string, name of an image file (PNG, GIF, PGM, and PPM) or ``\"nopic\"``, "
"or ``None``"
msgstr ""
"um string, um nome de um arquivo de imagem (PNG, GIF, PGM e PPM) ou "
"``\"nopic\"``, ou ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1644
msgid ""
"Set background image or return name of current backgroundimage.  If "
"*picname* is a filename, set the corresponding image as background.  If "
"*picname* is ``\"nopic\"``, delete background image, if present.  If "
"*picname* is ``None``, return the filename of the current backgroundimage. ::"
msgstr ""
"Configura a imagem de fundo ou retorna nome da imagem de fundo atual. Se "
"*picname* for um nome de arquivo, definirá a imagem correspondente como "
"plano de fundo. Se *picname* for ``\"nopic\"``, exclui a imagem de fundo, "
"caso haja. Se *picname* for ``None``, retorna o nome do arquivo da imagem de "
"fundo atual:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1649
msgid ""
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"'nopic'\n"
">>> screen.bgpic(\"landscape.gif\")\n"
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"\"landscape.gif\""
msgstr ""
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"'nopic'\n"
">>> screen.bgpic(\"landscape.gif\")\n"
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"\"landscape.gif\""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1660
msgid ""
"This TurtleScreen method is available as a global function only under the "
"name ``clearscreen``.  The global function ``clear`` is a different one "
"derived from the Turtle method ``clear``."
msgstr ""
"Este método de TurtleScreen está disponível como uma função global somente "
"sob o nome ``clearscreen``. A função global ``clear`` é derivada de forma "
"diferente do método de Turtle ``clear`` ."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1667
msgid ""
"Delete all drawings and all turtles from the TurtleScreen.  Reset the now "
"empty TurtleScreen to its initial state: white background, no background "
"image, no event bindings and tracing on."
msgstr ""
"Remove todos os desenhos e todas as tartarugas da TurtleScreen. Redefine a "
"TurtleScreen, agora vazia, para seu estado inicial: fundo branco, sem imagem "
"de fundo, sem vínculos de eventos e rastreamento ativado."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1676
msgid ""
"This TurtleScreen method is available as a global function only under the "
"name ``resetscreen``.  The global function ``reset`` is another one derived "
"from the Turtle method ``reset``."
msgstr ""
"Este método de TurtleScreen está disponível como uma função global somente "
"com o nome ``resetscreen``. A função global ``reset`` é outra derivada do "
"método de Turtle ``reset`` ."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1683
msgid "Reset all turtles on the screen to their initial state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1688
msgid "positive integer, new width of canvas in pixels"
msgstr "positivo inteiro, a nova largura da tela em pixels"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1689
msgid "positive integer, new height of canvas in pixels"
msgstr "positivo inteiro, a nova altura da tela em pixels"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1690
msgid "colorstring or color-tuple, new background color"
msgstr "Uma string com a cor ou uma tupla, a nova cor de fundo"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1692
msgid ""
"If no arguments are given, return current (canvaswidth, canvasheight).  Else "
"resize the canvas the turtles are drawing on.  Do not alter the drawing "
"window.  To observe hidden parts of the canvas, use the scrollbars. With "
"this method, one can make visible those parts of a drawing which were "
"outside the canvas before."
msgstr ""
"Se nenhum argumento for fornecido, retorna o atual (canvaswidth, "
"canvasheight). Caso contrário, redimensiona a tela em que as tartarugas "
"estão desenhadas. Não altera a janela de desenho. Para observar as partes "
"ocultas da tela, use as barras de rolagem. Com este método, é possível "
"tornar visíveis as partes de um desenho que antes estavam fora da tela."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1698
msgid ""
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(400, 300)\n"
">>> screen.screensize(2000,1500)\n"
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(2000, 1500)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(400, 300)\n"
">>> screen.screensize(2000,1500)\n"
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(2000, 1500)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1707
msgid "e.g. to search for an erroneously escaped turtle ;-)"
msgstr "Por exemplo, para procurar uma tartaruga que escapou por engano ;-)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1717
msgid ""
"Set up a user-defined coordinate system. *llx* and *lly* are the x and y "
"coordinates of the lower left corner of the canvas. *urx* and *ury* are the "
"x and y coordinates of the upper right corner. Switch to mode \"world\" if "
"necessary, which performs a reset. If mode \"world\" is already active, all "
"drawings are redrawn according to the new coordinates. In user-defined "
"coordinate systems, angles may appear distorted, see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1724
msgid ""
">>> screen.reset()\n"
">>> screen.setworldcoordinates(-50,-7.5,50,7.5)\n"
">>> for _ in range(72):\n"
"...     left(10)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for _ in range(8):\n"
"...     left(45); fd(2)   # a regular octagon"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.reset()\n"
">>> screen.setworldcoordinates(-50,-7.5,50,7.5)\n"
">>> for _ in range(72):\n"
"...     left(10)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for _ in range(8):\n"
"...     left(45); fd(2)   # a regular octagon"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1745
msgid "Animation control"
msgstr "Controle da animação"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1749
msgid ""
"Temporarily turn off turtle animation. The code inside the :keyword:`with` "
"block is not animated. Once the block is exited, the drawing appears. This "
"is useful for drawing complex shapes where even the fastest speed setting is "
"too slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1754
msgid ""
">>> with screen.no_animation():\n"
"...     for dist in range(2, 400, 2):\n"
"...         fd(dist)\n"
"...         rt(90)"
msgstr ""
">>> with screen.no_animation():\n"
"...     for dist in range(2, 400, 2):\n"
"...         fd(dist)\n"
"...         rt(90)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1767 ../../library/turtle.rst:1785
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1786
msgid "a nonnegative integer or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1769
msgid ""
"Return or set the drawing delay in milliseconds. This is approximately the "
"time interval between two consecutive canvas updates. The longer the drawing "
"delay, the slower the animation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1773
msgid ""
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"10\n"
">>> screen.delay(5)\n"
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"5"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"10\n"
">>> screen.delay(5)\n"
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"5"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1788
msgid ""
"Turn turtle animation on or off and set the drawing delay. If *n* is given, "
"only every n-th regular screen update is performed, which can be used to "
"speed up the drawing of complex graphics. If *n* is 0, animation is turned "
"off and the screen is only updated by calling :func:`update`. If *delay* is "
"given, it sets the drawing delay, see :func:`delay`. When called without "
"arguments, return the current value of *n*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1795
msgid ""
">>> screen.tracer(8, 25)\n"
">>> dist = 2\n"
">>> for i in range(200):\n"
"...     fd(dist)\n"
"...     rt(90)\n"
"...     dist += 2"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.tracer(8, 25)\n"
">>> dist = 2\n"
">>> for i in range(200):\n"
"...     fd(dist)\n"
"...     rt(90)\n"
"...     dist += 2"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1808
msgid "Perform a TurtleScreen update. To be used when tracer is turned off."
msgstr ""
"Executa uma atualização do TurtleScreen. Para ser usado quando o rastreador "
"estiver desligado."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1810
msgid "See also the RawTurtle/Turtle method :func:`speed`."
msgstr "Veja também o método RawTurtle/Turtle :func:`speed`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1814
msgid "Using screen events"
msgstr "Usando os eventos de tela"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1818
msgid ""
"Set focus on TurtleScreen (in order to collect key-events).  Dummy arguments "
"are provided in order to be able to pass :func:`listen` to the onclick "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Define o foco no TurtleScreen (para coletar eventos-chave). Argumentos "
"fictícios são fornecidos para que seja possível passar :func:`listen` para o "
"método onclick."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1825 ../../library/turtle.rst:1845
msgid "a function with no arguments or ``None``"
msgstr "uma função sem argumentos ou ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1826 ../../library/turtle.rst:1846
msgid "a string: key (e.g. \"a\") or key-symbol (e.g. \"space\")"
msgstr ""
"uma string: uma tecla (por exemplo, \"a\") ou o nome de uma tecla (por "
"exemplo, \"space\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1828
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to key-release event of key.  If *fun* is ``None``, event "
"bindings are removed. Remark: in order to be able to register key-events, "
"TurtleScreen must have the focus. (See method :func:`listen`.)"
msgstr ""
"Vincula *fun* ao evento de liberação da tecla. Se *fun* for ``None``, as "
"ligações de eventos serão removidas. Observação: para poder registrar "
"eventos-chave, o TurtleScreen deve ter o foco. (Veja o método :func:"
"`listen`.)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1832
msgid ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...     lt(60)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"
msgstr ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...     lt(60)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1848
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to key-press event of key if key is given, or to any key-press-"
"event if no key is given. Remark: in order to be able to register key-"
"events, TurtleScreen must have focus. (See method :func:`listen`.)"
msgstr ""
"Vincula *fun* ao evento de pressionamento de tecla se a tecla for fornecida, "
"ou a qualquer evento de pressionamento de tecla se nenhuma tecla for "
"fornecida. Observação: para poder registrar eventos-chave, o TurtleScreen "
"deve ter foco. (Veja o método :func:`listen`.)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1853
msgid ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"
msgstr ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1870
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-click events on this screen. *fun* is called with the "
"coordinates of the clicked point on the canvas. If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed. *btn* is the number of the mouse button and "
"defaults to 1, the left mouse button. If *add* is ``True``, a new binding is "
"added, otherwise it replaces a former binding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1876
msgid ""
"Example for a TurtleScreen instance named ``screen`` and a Turtle instance "
"named ``turtle``:"
msgstr ""
"Exemplo de uma instância de TurtleScreen chamada ``screen`` e uma instância "
"de Turtle chamada ``turtle``:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1879
msgid ""
">>> screen.onclick(turtle.goto) # Subsequently clicking into the "
"TurtleScreen will\n"
">>>                             # make the turtle move to the clicked "
"point.\n"
">>> screen.onclick(None)        # remove event binding again"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.onclick(turtle.goto) # Em seguida, clicar no TurtleScreen\n"
">>>                             # fará a tartaruga se mover até o ponto "
"clicado.\n"
">>> screen.onclick(None)        # remove associação de evento novamente"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1887
msgid ""
